@* The CAI-measured mark for one period — who earned it, and exactly why anybody did not.

   ★★ THE PAGE IS THE ACCOUNTABILITY. A mark that can be pulled is power over a competitor's marketing, and
   pulling one is far more newsworthy than granting one. So the four conditions, the fact each one READS, and the
   named condition that failed are all here: a withheld mark that only said "not qualified" would be an
   unreviewable veto wearing a public face.

   ★★ AND IT IS NOT A QUALITY BADGE. Three of the four conditions are about process — a tool with a poor rate
   that ran the published draw, submitted in time and published in full earns it. Said on the page, because a
   reader who assumes otherwise reads a withheld mark as a verdict on the tool.

   ★ Reads the store directly: this IS CAI, so an HTTP call to its own API would be a second path to the same
   rows and one more thing that can disagree. *@
@page "/noise/mark"
@page "/noise/mark/{Period}"
@using System.Globalization
@using Cai.Web.Noise
@inject INoiseStore Store

<PageTitle>CAI — @ComplianceMark.Label @Period</PageTitle>

@if (Period is not { Length: > 0 })
{
    @* ★ An index, so the mark is reachable without knowing a period — the same reason /noise/record has one. *@
    var periods = Store.PublishedPeriods().Concat(Store.JudgedPeriods())
        .Distinct(StringComparer.Ordinal)
        .OrderByDescending(p => p, StringComparer.Ordinal)
        .ToList();

    <div class="hero"><div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">@ComplianceMark.Label</p>
        <h1>The mark, by period</h1>
        <p class="lede">
            Who ran each period under the published method, and — where the mark is withheld — which condition
            did not hold.
        </p>
    </div></div>

    <section data-region="mark-index"><div class="wrap">
        @if (periods.Count == 0)
        {
            <p class="muted"><strong>No period has been measured yet.</strong> That is an absence, not a mark.</p>
        }
        else
        {
            <ul>
                @foreach (var p in periods)
                {
                    <li><a href="@($"/noise/mark/{p}")">@p</a></li>
                }
            </ul>
        }
    </div></section>

    return;
}

@{
    var deadline = NoiseCorpus.Draws.TryGetValue(Period!, out var draw) ? draw.SubmissionsCloseAt : null;
    var published = Store.LatestPublication(Period!) is not null;

    var marks = Store.ListSubmissions(Period!)
        .GroupBy(r => r.Tool, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
        .OrderBy(g => g.Key, StringComparer.Ordinal)
        .Select(g =>
        {
            var best = g.OrderByDescending(r => r.Accepted).ThenBy(r => r.ReceivedAt).First();

            return ComplianceMark.Evaluate(g.Key, Period!, new MarkInputs(
                RanAgainstTheHoldout: best.Accepted && best.CoveredRepositories > 0,
                SubmittedBeforeTheDeadline: deadline is not { } closes || best.ReceivedAt <= closes,
                RunReproduces: best.Accepted,
                NumbersPublishedInFull: published));
        })
        .ToList();
}

<div class="hero"><div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">@ComplianceMark.Label</p>
    <h1>@Period</h1>
    <p class="lede">
        Who ran this period under the published method, and — where the mark is withheld — exactly which
        condition did not hold and what fact decided it.
    </p>
</div></div>

<section data-region="marks"><div class="wrap">
    <h2>Participants</h2>

    @if (marks.Count == 0)
    {
        <p class="muted">
            <strong>No tool has submitted for this period.</strong> That is an absence — there is no mark to
            state either way.
        </p>
    }
    else
    {
        <table class="lenses">
            <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Mark</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var m in marks)
                {
                    <tr>
                        <td class="mono">@m.Tool</td>
                        <td>
                            <span class="pill @(m.Granted ? "upheld" : "open")">
                                @(m.Granted ? ComplianceMark.Label : "Withheld")
                            </span>
                        </td>
                        <td class="muted">
                            @if (m.Granted)
                            {
                                <text>
                                    Ran the published draw, submitted in time, passed every verification check,
                                    and published in full.
                                </text>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                @* ★★ THE CONDITION AND ITS REASON, never a summary. This is the message a
                                   competitor reads about itself in public, and "did not qualify" is one nobody
                                   can act on or contest. *@
                                foreach (var f in m.Failing)
                                {
                                    <div><strong class="mono">@f.Condition</strong> — @f.Why</div>
                                }
                            }
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    }
</div></section>

<section data-region="conditions"><div class="wrap">
    <h2>The four conditions, and what each one reads</h2>
    <table class="lenses">
        <thead><tr><th>Condition</th><th>Decided by</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var c in ComplianceMark.Conditions)
            {
                <tr><td class="mono">@c.Name</td><td class="muted">@c.Reads</td></tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>

    @if (deadline is { } closes2)
    {
        <p class="muted">
            Submissions for this period closed
            @closes2.UtcDateTime.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture). The deadline is signed with
            the draw: one that could move afterwards would not be a deadline.
        </p>
    }

    <div class="callout">
        <strong>It is free, and it is not a quality badge.</strong>
        @ComplianceMark.ChangeRule
        <br /><br />
        Three of the four conditions are about process: a tool with a poor noise rate that ran the published
        draw, submitted in time and published in full earns the mark. It states that the measurement happened
        properly — the published rate states how it went.
        <br /><br />
        <span class="muted">@ComplianceMark.AppealRoute</span>
    </div>
</div></section>

@code {
    /// <summary>The period, <c>yyyy-MM</c>.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Period { get; set; }
}
